     "question": "The pd is adjusted until the ammeter reads zero; the voltmeter reads 3.59 V. The UV frequency is 2.00 x 10^15 Hz. Calculate the work function in joules.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "Work function = 7.5 x 10^-19 J",
     "steps": [
      "At zero current the stopping pd gives the maximum kinetic energy: Ek = e V = 1.60 x 10^-19 C x 3.59 V = 5.74 x 10^-19 J.",
      "Photon energy E = h f = 6.63 x 10^-34 J s x 2.00 x 10^15 Hz = 1.33 x 10^-18 J.",
      "Einstein's equation: hf = phi + Ek, so phi = hf - Ek.",
      "phi = 1.33 x 10^-18 J - 5.74 x 10^-19 J = 7.5 x 10^-19 J."
     ],
