     "question": "Photons of energy 4.75 eV are incident on a metal with work function 6.30 x 10^-19 J. Show the maximum speed of emitted electrons is about 5.3 x 10^5 m s^-1.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "v_max = 5.3 x 10^5 m s^-1",
     "steps": [
      "Photon energy hf = 4.75 eV = 4.75 x 1.60 x 10^-19 J = 7.60 x 10^-19 J.",
      "Einstein's equation: Ek(max) = hf - phi = 7.60 x 10^-19 J - 6.30 x 10^-19 J = 1.30 x 10^-19 J.",
      "Ek = (1/2) m v^2, so v = sqrt(2 Ek / m) with m = 9.11 x 10^-31 kg.",
      "v = sqrt(2 x 1.30 x 10^-19 / 9.11 x 10^-31) = 5.3 x 10^5 m s^-1."
     ],
