     "question": "Two resistors each of resistance R are connected to a battery of e.m.f. E and internal resistance r, first in series (A) then in parallel (B). Which arrangement gives the greater terminal p.d.?",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "Series arrangement A gives the greater terminal p.d.",
     "steps": [
      "Terminal p.d. V = E x R_ext / (R_ext + r), where R_ext is the external resistance.",
      "Series: R_ext = 2R, so V_A = 2RE / (2R + r).",
      "Parallel: R_ext = R/2, so V_B = (R/2)E / (R/2 + r) = RE / (R + 2r).",
      "Ratio V_A / V_B = 2(R + 2r) / (2R + r) = (2R + 4r) / (2R + r), which is greater than 1 because 4r > r.",
      "So V_A > V_B: the series arrangement gives the greater terminal p.d. (more external resistance means less lost to internal resistance)."
     ],
