     "question": "Derive Lawrence's expression for the time t for a particle of charge q and mass m to complete one circular path in a uniform magnetic field of flux density B.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "t = 2 pi m / (B q)",
     "steps": [
      "The magnetic force provides the centripetal force: B q v = m v^2 / r.",
      "Rearrange to get the radius: r = m v / (B q).",
      "The time for one circuit is the circumference divided by the speed: t = 2 pi r / v.",
      "Substitute r: t = 2 pi (m v / (B q)) / v, so the speed cancels.",
      "Result: t = 2 pi m / (B q), independent of speed and radius."
     ],
