     "question": "Calculate the length of a simple pendulum that swings from one extreme position to the other in exactly 1.00 s.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "Length = 0.99 m.",
     "steps": [
      "One swing from one extreme to the other is half a period, so the full period T = 2.00 s.",
      "For a simple pendulum T = 2 pi sqrt(L/g), so L = g T^2 / (4 pi^2).",
      "L = 9.81 x 2.00^2 / (4 pi^2) = 39.24 / 39.48 = 0.99 m."
     ],
