     "question": "A 0.35 kg mass on a spring has period 0.95 s. After an extra mass is added the period is 1.15 s. Calculate the added mass.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "Added mass = 0.16 kg.",
     "steps": [
      "Period T = 2 pi sqrt(m/k), so T^2 is proportional to m with k constant.",
      "(T2 / T1)^2 = m_total / m1, so m_total = 0.35 x (1.15 / 0.95)^2 = 0.35 x 1.465 = 0.513 kg.",
      "Added mass = 0.513 - 0.350 = 0.16 kg.",
      "The added mass is about 0.16 kg."
     ],
