     "question": "A woman of mass 67 kg oscillates on an elastic rope with period 1.50 s. A second person of mass 72 kg is then attached and the same rope is used. Calculate the new period.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "Period = 2.16 s.",
     "steps": [
      "The rope's stiffness is constant: k = 4 pi^2 m / T^2 = 4 pi^2 x 67 / 1.50^2 = 1.18 x 10^3 N m-1.",
      "The new total mass is m = 67 + 72 = 139 kg.",
      "T = 2 pi sqrt(m / k) = 2 pi sqrt(139 / 1176) = 2.16 s.",
      "So the period of the two people is 2.16 s."
     ],
