     "question": "Show that the current radius of the Sun is about 7.0 x 10^8 m, given L = 3.83 x 10^26 W and T = 5780 K.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "R = 6.9 x 10^8 m, about 7.0 x 10^8 m",
     "steps": [
      "Black body radiation: L = 4 pi R^2 sigma T^4 (Stefan-Boltzmann law).",
      "sigma = 5.67 x 10^-8 W m^-2 K^-4; T^4 = 5780^4 = 1.12 x 10^15 K^4.",
      "R^2 = L / (4 pi sigma T^4) = 3.83 x 10^26 / (4 pi x 5.67 x 10^-8 x 1.12 x 10^15) = 4.82 x 10^17 m^2.",
      "R = sqrt(4.82 x 10^17) = 6.9 x 10^8 m, about 7.0 x 10^8 m."
     ],
